<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Battle of Panipat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1526">1526</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Battle of Panipat was fought in 1526 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-lodi">Ibrahim Lodi</a>, the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. Babur's use of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">field artillery</a> and cavalry tactics defeated a much larger army, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> and founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-panipat.jpg" alt="First Battle of Panipat" width="263" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ẓahīr ud-Dīn Muḥammad Bābur (1483-1530); It contains 30 mostly full-page miniatures in fine Mughal style by at least two different artists. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_battle_of_Panipat_and_the_death_of_Sultan_Ibr%C4%81h%C4%ABm,_the_last_of_the_L%C5%8Dd%C4%AB_Sultans_of_Delhi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
